\section{Estimator and intervals}
\label{sec:method}

The estimator we use to measure headroom is an AIPW-type, cross-fitted version of \eqref{eq:est}; it is textbook double machine learning with a known propensity \citep{chernozhukov2018double} and is not offered as a new method. Split the labeled records into $K$ folds. Fit $\hat g^{(-k)}$ on the labeled records outside fold $k$ (a calibrator of $Y$ on $Z$: isotonic or spline regression on $f$ for T1, gradient boosting on $(f,X)$ for T2), and let $\bar g$ be the average of the fold models. With out-of-fold residuals $h_i=Y_i-\hat g^{(-k(i))}(Z_i)$,
\begin{align}
